From 56d45ef4915bf8f404eb6a964a3e77fac8437e8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gemini experiment archive <experiment@invalid.example>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 07:52:25 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] wlan: capture native firmware buffer and sections

Carry a successful file-read ordinal and its borrowed buffer through the
probe and adapter calls to the divided loader. Check the exact pointer,
extent and binding before reading payload bytes. Bound this experiment to
the retained 411632-byte, four-section MT6797 image layout.

Hash the actual input through the native SHA-256 shash interface, record
ordered section metadata and the native return, and reject capture when
the closing digest differs. Keep the hash transform until every native
return path releases it. This adds one crypto allocation and at most two
whole-buffer hash calls; it does not prove immutability between hashes.

Native transfers, EMI operations and return values remain unchanged. The
read mapping depends on its explicit failure-handling predecessor. Failed
capture stops observation, without repairing or retrying the native path.

This is an unselected experiment, not an upstream ABI or boot candidate.
Whole-image lifetime, EMI/OFF capture, recovery and acquisition timing
remain unfinished. The synthetic archive identity supplies
no author certification.
